ga48(){return"SimplyMind is a local, offline-first mind map. Maps stay on this device as JSON. This guide covers the home list, the canvas editor, starters, export, and install."},
ga47(){return"Home: your maps"},
ga46(){return"The home screen lists every mind map on this device, newest first. Tap a map to open the editor. Use the \u22ee menu on a row to rename, duplicate, move to a category, export JSON, or delete.\n\nThe + New mind map button starts a title, starter, and layout. Import JSON from the folder icon in the top bar."},
ga4_(){return"Create: starter and layout"},
ga3Z(){return"Starter is the content you begin with. Blank is one central node. PRD is a product-outline (problem, goals, users, requirements, scope). Entities is a sketch of related tables (User, Account, Order, Product) with fields as children \u2014 not a full database diagram.\n\nLayout is how nodes sit: Map (drag freely), List (outline), Step (numbered flow), Graph (around the parent). You can change layout later in the editor. Picking PRD suggests List; Entities suggests Graph."},
ga41(){return"Editor: nodes and branches"},
ga40(){return"Tap a node to select it and show the toolbar. Double-tap to edit text. + adds a child (in Map mode it finds free space near siblings). Drag a non-root node onto another to reparent. Promote (\u21c8) makes a node a sibling of its parent.\n\nIn List/Step/Graph, use the arrow buttons to reorder siblings. Branch template overrides layout for that subtree. Status (none / in progress / done) and color live on each node. Map settings (tune icon) change padding between text and the box."},
ga3Y(){return"Canvas: zoom and focus"},
ga3X(){return"Pinch or use + / \u2212 to zoom. Fit-all shows every node on screen (also used when you first open a map). Focus mode (fullscreen icon) hides the top bar and overlays so you can think on a wider canvas. The hint at the bottom summarizes drag, promote, and double-tap."},
ga4e(){return"Categories"},
ga4d(){return"Maps start in Home. After many maps, SimplyMind offers categories. Create them from More or the chip row. Filter with All / Home / your names. Move a map from its \u22ee menu. Deleting a category sends maps back to Home; it does not delete the maps."},
ga43(){return"Export, import, and share"},
ga42(){return"In the editor, the share menu exports JSON (editable backup), PNG (picture of the whole map), or PDF. JSON import is on the home screen. PNG/PDF redraw the full tree \u2014 not a screenshot of the current zoom."},
ga4c(){return"Web, install, and offline"},
ga4b(){return"On the website you can Add to Home Screen. After one online visit, the app can open without internet (service worker). Maps stay in local storage. Open the site on HTTPS. iOS may clear unused site data after weeks \u2014 export JSON if you need a backup. Native Android/iOS builds store data on the device without that web limit."},
ga4a(){return"Language"},
ga49(){return"More \u2192 Language: follow the device, English, or Bahasa Indonesia. Menus and this guide change; text you typed in nodes does not."},
ga45(){return"Feedback and legal"},
ga44(){return"More \u2192 Send feedback opens WhatsApp with a short pre-filled message. Privacy Policy and DMCA are in the same menu."},
